---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Bar from '../components/Bar.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
import { Fragment } from 'astro/jsx-runtime';
import TerminalWindow from '../components/TerminalWindow.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
		<style>
		img {
			border-radius: 100px;
			border: 2px solid var(--white);
			float: right;
		}


		@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
			img{
				scale: 1;
				transition: scale 2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 0.35, 0, 1.15);
			}

			img:hover{
				scale: 1.1;
				animation: rotateAnimation 1s ease-in-out 0.3s infinite;
			}

			@keyframes rotateAnimation{
				0% {
					rotate: 0deg;
				}
				100% {
					rotate: 360deg;
				}
			}
		}


		h1{
			padding-bottom: 1em;
		}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Bar title={SITE_TITLE} />
		<TerminalWindow>
			<main transition:animate="fade">
				<h1>
					About Me
				</h1>
				<a href="https://github.com/Cyanistic">
					<img src="/me.png" alt="" />
				</a>
				<h2>
					Cyanistic
				</h2>
				<p>
					Hi there! I'm Cyanistic, a software engineer and tech enthusiast living in the US. I graduated Summa Cum Laude from Florida International University with a B.S. in Computer Science.
				</p>
				<p>
					When it comes to programming, Rust is my language of choice.
					I love the memory safety features and the concise syntax, which makes it a breeze to write clean and efficient code.
					I've had the opportunity to work on several projects using Rust, in fact, all of the application listed on the projects page are written in rust.
					In addition to Rust, I'm also proficient in other languages such as Javascript, TypeScript, and Python.
					I'm always looking to expand my skill set and learn new technologies, so if you have any recommendations, feel free to share!
					As a software engineer, I'm passionate about building platform infrastructure: tools that let other engineers move faster and make fewer mistakes.
					I believe in continuous learning and improvement, and I'm always looking for ways to improve my craft.
				</p>
				<p>

					When I'm not coding, you can find me gaming on my Linux machine.
					I'm a fan of rhythm games like Beat Saber, and I also enjoy playing other types of games like strategy and adventure games.
					I'm also a big fan of free and open-source software.
					I believe that software should be free and open to everyone, and I'm always happy to contribute to projects that align with these values.
					If you're looking for a dedicated and detail-oriented software engineer with a passion for Rust and Linux, then you've come to the right place!
					Feel free to reach out to me through my contact page.
					I'm always excited to connect with other tech enthusiasts and discuss the latest developments in the world of software engineering.
				</p>
			</main>
		</TerminalWindow>
	</body>
</html>

